      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "All seven current selections agree with their own captured worked solutions and are mathematically correct. q-132240: y=x² intersects y=4 at x=±2, so vertical slices have −2≤x≤2 and x²≤y≤4. q-132289: integrating first in y gives ∫₀¹x(x−x³)dx=1/3−1/5=2/15. q-81778: horizontal slices have 0≤y≤2 and 0≤x≤y, giving ∫₀²y³dy=4, equivalent to MA's vertical-slice calculation. q-132402: the depicted upper region has 0≤y≤2 and y²−4≤x≤4−y². q-132410: solving the lines for x gives left boundary y/2−2 and right boundary 4−y over 0≤y≤4. q-132512: the curves intersect at y=±1; the depicted region above the x-axis uses 0≤y≤1 and y²≤x≤2−y². q-81294: y=2−y² has roots −2 and 1; the depicted upper region uses 0≤y≤1 and y≤x≤2−y². Its problem text calls x=2−y² a line, although it is a parabola; this terminology error does not affect the correct answer or worked bounds. Bracketed inner integrals and unbracketed repeated integrals represent the same integrations.",
